      "_formatNotes": [
        "Wire frame layout override for THIS analyzer's Format Configuration (Run Date/Time ON, Type ON, no Dilution/Reagent/ISE, Zero Suppress ON; Rack ID 4 / Online Test No. 3 / Result 6 / Flags 2). Derived and byte-verified from the real R/S/D frames in the eLab logs.",
        "The header is 58 chars (vs the AU480 default 64): after the 7-digit barcode sit '    E' + a 14-digit Run Date/Time timestamp before the result groups. Field widths here make auHeaderWidth() = 2+4+2+4+1+26+19 = 58 and put the barcode in the right-justified sampleId(26) field. Result group = testNo(3)+result(6)+marks(2) = 11, no diluent.",
        "responseDemographics=false: the analyzer's S order-response is just '…barcode␠␠␠␠E<testNos>' with NO M00000+patient-name block (confirmed against eLab's S frames, e.g. 'S 000801 0220 ... 9153004    E014'). Sending the default demographics block would push the Online Test Nos to the wrong offset and the analyzer would run the wrong assays."
      ],
      "source": "Rohtak DxC 700 AU. Online Test No. table, Protocol and Format read off the analyzer's Configuration > Online screens (2026-07-26), cross-validated against the eLab Assist serial logs (logDetails/logINMessage 22-26 Jul 2026). Noble LIS targets resolved against the live catalog; shared analytes reuse the IDs already verified on the Karnal AU480 (same Noble DB), DxC-only analytes (CK, LDH, Lipase, Amylase, Mg, LDL, HbA1c) resolved and checked on 2026-07-26.",
      "mappingsSummary": { "total": 38, "mapped": 31, "unmapped": 7 },
      "_protocolNotes": [
        "Connection is SERIAL RS-232, 9600 8-N-1, STX/ETX framing, no BCC checksum (Protocol screen: Character 8/None/1, Start 02h STX, End 03h ETX, 9600 bps, Class B, BCC unchecked). eLab currently drives it over a serial write port.",
        "Format (Format Configuration screen): Rack ID 4 digits, Online Test No. 3 digits, Result 6 digits, 2 flags, Run Date/Time on, Zero Suppress on — i.e. the default Synapse AU frame layout. Verified against real D-blocks e.g. 'D 001006 0187 ... E20260722000759 001  3.33  009 0.335 ...' where each pair is testNo(3)+value(6).",
        "Host query is ON and realtime (Setup screen: Routine First-Run/Rerun Test Order Receive = Realtime). The analyzer sends R-blocks (barcode) and expects an S-block carrying the ordered Online Test Nos; enable Host Query in Synapse.",
        "The analyzer's numbering (see onlineTestMenu) is DIFFERENT from the Karnal AU480 — e.g. here 003=ALT, 005=AST, 028=BUN, whereas Karnal used 007=AST, 008=ALT. This per-site table MUST be applied or the fail-closed AU gate will (correctly) refuse to write."
      ],
      "_mappingNotes": [
        "BUN/UREA measurand check (2026-07-26): the DxC test 028 is named BUN1N, but the value it transmits is the UREA value, not BUN. Verified on live samples — SID 9143887 sent 18.88 on test 028, and Noble stored 18.88 raw in the Urea field (BI224) while its BUN field (BI056) holds 8.8 = 18.88/2.14. So map test 028 -> Urea BI224 with NO conversion (Noble derives BUN itself). This matches how eLab and the Karnal AU already behave.",
        "Bilirubin: the DxC is configured for the DCA method (012 DBC direct, 024 TBC total) — confirmed the only bilirubin numbers in the logs. The BuBc-method channels (011 DBB, 023 TBB) are configured on the analyzer but never run, so they are left in the decode table (onlineTestMenu) but NOT mapped.",
        "Albumin (001) and Total Protein (025) map to the Noble composite 'Total protein (with albumin and globulin)' (BI213) params 676/678, reusing the Karnal-verified targets on this same Noble DB. The repository's tier fallbacks also fill standalone Albumin/TP rows when a sample ordered them directly.",
        "Serum-index (096 LIH), and the HbA1c intermediate channels 101 (T-Hb) / 102 (A1c) are decode-only intermediates, not reportables — kept in onlineTestMenu, left unmapped. Urine Protein (030) and Microalbumin (031) are configured but not run on this analyzer in the captured period; left in the table, unmapped, pending a lab decision on their spot-urine Noble targets.",
        "GLU (014) and RF (022) use Synapse's AU variant groups: the single analyzer channel fills whichever ordered variant (glucose Fasting/PP/Random; RA-factor method) the sample carried."
      ],
