      "source": "Rohtak Getein MAGICL 6200. HL7 v2.3.1 over MLLP, captured from the eLab Assist logs (06-08 Aug 2026): QRY^Q02 host query (barcode in QRD-8) answered by QCK+DSR^Q03, ORU^R01 result upload ACKed. Identical getein dialect to the Delhi 6000i — only the assay item-ids differ. 14 assays actually in use; every Noble target reused from the Delhi MAGICL (same Noble DB) and re-confirmed on 2026-08-08.",
      "mappingsSummary": { "total": 14, "mapped": 14, "unmapped": 0 },
      "_mappingNotes": [
        "Analyte key (instrumentCode) is the MAGICL numeric assay item-id from OBX-3; the analyzer also puts the friendly name in OBX-4, so decoding is unambiguous. The 6200 uses 4-digit ids (TSH=1018, T3=1019, …) — the 6000i's ids + 1000 for most, EXCEPT 25-OH-VD which is 1151 (not 1042). Read verbatim from the ORU frames, not inferred.",
        "Same getein HL7 flow as the Delhi 6000i, so no driver change was needed — only this per-site item-id -> Noble map. The host query answers QRY^Q02 (QRD-8 barcode) with the ordered item-ids in the DSR, and ACKs each ORU^R01.",
        "UNIT TRAPS, both verified against what eLab actually wrote to Noble for THIS analyzer's SIDs (2026-08-08): FT3 (1021) arrives pmol/L and Noble stores pg/mL — eLab converts x0.651, and Synapse's units.ts does the same conversion for FT3, so it matches (e.g. SID 9282585 wire ~5.4 pmol/L -> Noble 3.54 pg/mL). FT4 (1022) arrives pmol/L and eLab stores it RAW in Noble's ng/L field (SID 9282585 wire 12.64 -> Noble 12.64), NO conversion; Synapse has no pmol/L->ng/L rule so it passes through raw too — matching eLab. Noble's FT4 'ng/L' label is nominal (the lab's reference range is set for the raw analyzer number); do not add a conversion without the lab's sign-off.",
        "Testosterone (1034) arrives ng/dL and Noble stores ng/dL — direct, matching the corrected Delhi/X3 Testosterone finding. T3 ng/mL, T4 ug/dL, TSH uIU/mL all map directly.",
        "Connection: getein analyzers dial the LIS as TCP client. Set the analyzer's HL7/Ethernet Server IP to this host's instrument-LAN IP and its port to match; Synapse listens as tcp-server on that port (8081 default, as at Delhi). Confirm the port on the analyzer's LIS screen. This is a SEPARATE instrument from the Rohtak DxC 700 AU (serial) in this same preset."
      ],
